{
  "version": 2,
  "cells": [
    {
      "kind": "markup",
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": [
        "# Rust\n",
        "\n",
        "Nothing about a Rust project is special-cased — `compiler` and `flags` default\n",
        "from the language of the cells, so an empty buildspec cell is enough.\n",
        "\n",
        "The one real difference is that **`rustc` compiles a crate root, not a file\n",
        "list**. The cell holding `fn main` is the root; every other cell is written into\n",
        "the build dir beside it and reached with `mod`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "language": "toml",
      "value": [
        "# Defaults for a rust project: rustc --edition=2021 -O\n",
        "compiler = \"rustc\"\n",
        "mode   = \"run\"\n",
        "output = \"greeter\"\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "language": "rust",
      "value": [
        "pub struct Greeter {\n",
        "    name: String,\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "impl Greeter {\n",
        "    pub fn new(name: &str) -> Self {\n",
        "        Self { name: name.to_string() }\n",
        "    }\n",
        "\n",
        "    pub fn greet(&self) -> String {\n",
        "        format!(\"hello, {}, from a compiler notebook\", self.name)\n",
        "    }\n",
        "}\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "role": "file",
        "filename": "greeter.rs"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "markup",
      "language": "markdown",
      "value": [
        "`mod greeter;` is what pulls the cell above into the crate. The file has to be\n",
        "named `greeter.rs` for that to work, which is exactly what the status bar on\n",
        "that cell shows."
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "code",
      "language": "rust",
      "value": [
        "mod greeter;\n",
        "\n",
        "use greeter::Greeter;\n",
        "\n",
        "fn main() {\n",
        "    let who = [\"world\", \"rustc\"];\n",
        "    for name in who {\n",
        "        println!(\"{}\", Greeter::new(name).greet());\n",
        "    }\n",
        "}\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "role": "file",
        "filename": "main.rs"
      }
    }
  ]
}
